---
description: How Last Day's agents are built. Apply when editing lastday/agents/.
globs: lastday/agents/**/*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

- Agents read and write the shared `Blackboard` only. To get work done by another agent, post a
  request with `bb.request(by, kind, system, detail, **payload)`; the Planner turns open requests into
  tasks for the next round. Request kinds the Planner handles: `corroborate`, `identity`, `retry_source`,
  `tacit`. Anything else is dropped with a reason.
- Query with `bb.sql(agent, purpose, sql, numeric=(...))`. It returns `None` when a source is down;
  handle that and carry on with lower confidence instead of raising.
- Record every decision with `bb.emit(agent, kind, summary, **data)`. The summary is shown verbatim in the
  UI trace, so write it as a plain sentence a manager can read.
- Evidence ids look like `<source>:<kind>:<ref>` and must be added with `bb.add_evidence(Evidence(...))`
  before anything cites them.
- Label changes need a reason in `area.history` (`{"round", "stage", "notes": [...]}`).
- After changing scoring or critique, run `python -m lastday eval --seeds 42 7 13 21` and compare with
  `samples/eval.json`.
